====================
JVM = Java Virtual Machine, we say java is platform independent because of JVM,
your OS works on hardware and JVM is in top of OS
We dont write a code that works directly on hardware or software, If you want to make it work you will need to run your code in JVM
when we say JAva is platform independent we can run it on any machine irrespective of OS the only think is the machine should have JVM
JVM only understnds bytecode
.java file=>compiler javac=>.class bytecode=>JVM=>MAchine code
JVM automatically handles:
Garbage collection (no manual memory free)
Heap & stack management
👉 JVM is the engine that runs Java bytecode and makes Java platform independent